  "name": "Answer customer questions on Telegram with Gemini and a Google Sheets FAQ",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "sticky-main",
      "name": "sticky-main",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1000,
        260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 880,
        "height": 620,
        "content": "## Answer customer questions on Telegram from your FAQ sheet\n\nA Gemini assistant answers your customers on Telegram from a FAQ you keep in Google Sheets. When a message needs a person (a booking, a complaint, a quote, or something the FAQ does not cover), a second Gemini call spots it and alerts you on Telegram. Every message is logged to a sheet.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. A customer writes to your Telegram bot.\n2. **Read the FAQ** loads your questions and answers, and **Your settings** adds your hours, services and address.\n3. **Answer from the FAQ** replies in the customer's language and remembers the last 10 messages. It does not make up answers.\n4. **Needs a person?** reads the question and the reply and decides if you should step in.\n5. Every exchange goes to your **Log** tab. When you are needed, you also get a Telegram alert.\n\n### How to set up\n\n- [ ] Create a bot with @BotFather and connect it to the three Telegram nodes.\n- [ ] Add a free Gemini API key from Google AI Studio to both Gemini nodes.\n- [ ] Make a **FAQ** tab (columns Question, Answer) and a **Log** tab (Time, Customer, Message, Reply, Needs a person).\n- [ ] Fill in **Your settings**, including your own Telegram chat ID and the sheet IDs.\n- [ ] Activate the workflow and send your bot a question.\n\n### How to customize\n\nEdit the categories in **Needs a person?** to choose what reaches you. New FAQ rows are used from the next message, no workflow edits needed."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
